Thai VAT invoice OCR (Tier 2). Return ONLY valid JSON object.

Required fields:
- invoice_number
- issuer_name
- net_amount_ex_vat
- total_amount

Optional fields (include only if visible):
- issuer_address (full address of issuer/seller)
- issuer_postal_code
- issuer_branch_id (branch number or "สำนักงานใหญ่")
- customer_name (name of buyer/customer)
- customer_address (full address of buyer/customer)
- customer_postal_code
- customer_branch_id (branch number or "สำนักงานใหญ่")
- credit_days
- credit_due_date (YYYY-MM-DD)
- is_vat_included (true/false/null)
- notes
- line_items (array of product/service items on the bill)

line_items format:
Each item is an object: {"description":"...","quantity":N,"unit_price":N,"total":N,"category":"..."}
- description: product/service name (Thai or English as shown)
- quantity: number of units (null if not shown)
- unit_price: price per unit (null if not shown)
- total: line total amount
- category: product category if identifiable (null otherwise)
Extract ALL visible line items from the document.

Rules:
- No guessing: missing => {"value":null,"confidence":0.3}
- Partially readable => confidence 0.4-0.7
- Raw numeric values only
- Do not calculate missing totals
- Keep string fields short (<=120 chars)
- Escape all internal double-quotes in string values

Return format:
{ "field_name": { "value": ..., "confidence": 0.0-1.0 } }
